      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Planning a corporate gala with such a diverse and large guest list is indeed a daunting task, but with a little bit of foresight and a lot of planning, you can turn this into a successful event. To manage the dietary requirements and avoid the \"chaos factor,\" consider implementing a few key strategies.\n\nFirst, establish a clear and detailed communication channel with your catering team. Make sure they understand the importance of avoiding cross-contamination, especially for guests with nut allergies. You could even consider having a dedicated \"goblin-free\" kitchen area for allergen-free dishes.\n\nNext, create a comprehensive guest list with all dietary preferences and restrictions clearly marked. This will help your catering team prepare the right dishes for everyone. You could also consider using a digital platform where guests can update their dietary needs closer to the event date.\n\nTo address the unpredictable elements, it's essential to have a contingency plan in place. This could include having extra ingredients on hand, a backup catering team, or even a few extra dishes prepared just in case. Think of it as having a \"goblin-proof\" plan to ensure that even if something goes wrong, you're prepared to handle it.\n\nLastly, don't forget to involve your guests in the planning process. You could send",
